{"id":"4616588c-91bc-48c9-9955-3f7c9c7e16ba","article_key":"doi:10.1016/j.cell.2026.09.037","title":"Comprehensive benchmarking of somatic mutation detection by the SMaHT Network","title_zh":"SMaHT网络对体细胞突变检测的全面基准评估","doi":"10.1016/j.cell.2026.09.037","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2026.09.037","abstract":"Somatic mosaicism is increasingly recognized as a fundamental feature of human biology, yet the detection of somatic mutations remains challenging. The Somatic Mosaicism across Human Tissues (SMaHT) Network conducted large-scale benchmarking experiments involving cell lines and donor tissues to evaluate sequencing technologies, experimental approaches, and computational methods for detecting different types of somatic mutations, generating community resources with >1,000× short-read and 100-400× long-read data for nine analyzed samples. We determined effective strategies for utilizing short- and long-read sequencing for mutation detection and demonstrated that using donor-specific and pangenome-inferred diploid assemblies improved calling, extending mutation catalogs to challenging genomic regions. We benchmarked six duplex technologies and showed that single-cell sequencing resolves cell-type-specific mutational patterns and heterogeneity. Our results indicate that bulk, single-cell, and duplex analyses are complementary and that leveraging all three provides comprehensive characterization of mosaicism within tissues. Together, these findings provide the scientific and clinical communities with a roadmap for accurate genome-wide somatic mutation analysis.","abstract_zh":"体细胞嵌合体在人体生物学中正被日益认可为一种基本特征，但体细胞突变的检测仍然具有挑战性。Somatic Mosaicism across Human Tissues（SMaHT）网络开展了大规模基准实验，涉及细胞系和供体组织，以评估不同测序技术、实验方法和计算方法在检测各种体细胞突变方面的性能，并为九个分析样本生成了超过1,000×的短读长读数据（100-400×）的社区资源。我们确定了利用短读和长读测序进行突变检测的有效策略，并证明使用供体特异性和泛基因组推断的二倍体组装可改进突变调用，将突变目录扩展到具有挑战性的基因组区域。我们对六种双重技术进行了基准测试，并显示单细胞测序能够解析细胞类型特异性的突变模式和异质性。我们的结果表明，批量、单细胞和双重分析是互补的，利用三者可全面表征组织内的嵌合体。综上所述，这些发现为科学和临床社区提供了准确全基因组体细胞突变分析的路线图。","snippet":"Somatic mosaicism is increasingly recognized as a fundamental feature of human biology, yet the detection of somatic mutations remains challenging. The Somatic Mosaicism across Human Tissues (SMaHT) Network conducted large-scale benchmarking experiments involving cell lines and donor tissues to evaluate sequencing technologies, experimental approaches, and computational methods for detecting different types of somat…","translated_at":"2026-10-16T23:34:06.596097Z","translation_model":"openai/gpt-oss-20b","source_category":"doi","article_type":"journal-article","volume":"189","issue":"21","published_at":"2026-10-01T00:00:00","acquired_at":"2026-10-15T19:43:22Z","display_date":"2026-10-15T19:43:22Z","display_date_source":"acquired","online_published_at":null,"print_published_at":"2026-10-01T00:00:00","first_author":"Alexej Abyzov","authors_text":"Alexej Abyzov, Abhiram Natu, Adam Voshall, Adriana E. Sedeño-Cortés, Aidan H. Burn, Alan P. Boyle, Alexander D. Veit, Alexander E. Urban, Alexandre Pellan Cheng, Alexi Runnels, Alisa Mo, Amooyla Srinivasa, Amy Leonardson, Andrea J. Kriz, Andrew B. Stergachis, Andrew J.C. Russell, Andrew J. Schroeder, Andrew R. D’Avino, Andrew Ruttenberg, Ann Caplin, Anna Minkina, Areum Cho, Arijit Panda, Aristotelis Tsirigos, Arnaz Maryam Tariq, Ayush Semwal, Azeet Narayan, Azra Hasan, Benjamin Costa, Benjamin K. Johnson, Benno Orr, Benpeng Miao, Bianca Morris, Bo Zhou, Boxun Zhao, Brad Demarest, Bradley E. Bernstein, Brandt A. Bessell, Brianne Carroll, Brianne E. Livermore, Caitlin N. Jacques, Camille Mumm, Carlos Mendez-Dorantes, Carolin Purman, Carrie Cibulskis, Casey Andrews, Catherine Potenski, Cesar Ferreyra-Mansilla, Chad Tomlinson, Charlotte Zhang, Chenghang Zong, Cheuk-Ting Law, Chia-Lin Wei, Chris Oliveira, Christian D. Frazar, Christina Missler, Christina Zakarian, Christopher A. Walsh, Christopher M. Grochowski, Christopher Walsh, Clara TaeHee Kim, Colleen P. Davis, Constantijn Scharlee, Corinne E. Sexton, Dan A. Landau